    {
      "id": "external.v2.verifier_policy_clarification",
      "title": "Verifier policy clarification: V2-10 Q1, Q2 and Q3 under exact policies and modes (verifier_policy_clarification_vectors.json)",
      "claim": "Each case runs under its exact policy and verification_time, as the dated clarification of VERIFICATION.md V2-10 (05/11/2026) decides. Under pq_only, classical lists and advisories that exclude ed25519 do not reject a hybrid bundle (Q1); a bundle, passport or checkpoint signature whose classical component fails verification while its PQ component verifies over those classical bytes is accepted (Q2), but a classical sig_b64 that is not canonical base64, or a classical kid that names no key, is rejected. In the other modes the same exclusions and signatures are rejected. Under classical_only and hybrid_preferred, PQ lists and advisories do not reject a bundle without a PQ component, while the hybrid bundle under the same policy is rejected (Q3). Every negative counts only if its positive control passed in the same run.",
      "limits": [
        "Opt-in: it does not change the default catalog (/1, 38 cases), the evidence catalog (/2, 241 cases), the admission catalog (/3, 140 cases) or the 74 cases of external.v2.verifier_policy.",
        "Two routine bases, routine_hybrid of verifier_policy_vectors.json and the classical-only routine bundle of bundle_vectors.json, bound by sha256: each requested mode is also the effective mode. The Q2 variants re-sign only a PQ component with the committed TEST-ONLY key; the scope variants change one value and keep every signature byte.",
        "Only the verdict is judged. Warnings are diagnostics: allow_classical_fallback_disable changes a warning, never a verdict. Rejection messages are not judged."
      ],
